module std where

-- countryFlag — derive a country's flag emoji from its ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code.
--
-- storage-as-effect Phase 3c (D5 slice 3). The flag was a denormalized `_flag`
-- field baked into every country-data.fenel row VALUE (3a baked it from the
-- retired `flag()` TS helper). There was NO Fenel definition of "flag from code"
-- — only the baked result, an ad-hoc encoding of a Fenel fact
-- ([[feedback_no_language_concept_in_ts]]). This is the real definition: the
-- projection is now the source of truth; the reference-data view materializes
-- `_flag` by calling it.
--
-- A flag emoji is structurally the two Regional-Indicator-Symbol letters for the
-- 2-letter code (US → 🇺 + 🇸 = 🇺🇸). `regionalIndicator` maps an uppercase letter
-- A..Z → its RI char 🇦..🇿 via a 26-branch cascade (the 26 RI chars are string
-- literals — NO char-ordinal native needed; same posture as crypto:uuidV4's
-- pure-over-literals composition). Codes in country-data.fenel are already
-- uppercase, so no case-fold is required.
--
-- The cascade is a single-line direct function body (the uuidVariantNibble /
-- clamp / compareGeoLevel precedent) — a multi-`else if` chain bound to a `let`
-- and then referenced by a LATER `let` trips the current Fenel parser (the
-- else-if grammar fence, parser-substrate territory); a standalone body sidesteps
-- it so this file stays Fenel-parser-driven (no FENCE_FALLBACK entry).
--
-- Composes std:slice (2-letter split) + std:concat (string concat over List Char,
-- String being `$opaque { repr: "string", pure: $list Char }`) + std:eq.
-- Pure — no IO, no native beyond the std string substrate.
--
-- This body is EXACTLY what a future value-parametric `Emojiable Country.emoji`
-- method will call (storage-as-effect 3c Option C, Rom 2026-06-19 — the
-- value-parametric-representations arc is deferred; this slice ships the
-- projection only, does NOT register an Emojiable instance).

@label "Regional indicator letter"
@description "Map an uppercase ASCII letter A..Z to its Regional Indicator Symbol emoji 🇦..🇿. Helper for std:countryFlag (storage-as-effect Phase 3c)."
@tags "geo" "country" "flag" "emoji" "storage-as-effect"
regionalIndicator : (c: String) -> String
regionalIndicator c = if c == "A" then "🇦" else if c == "B" then "🇧" else if c == "C" then "🇨" else if c == "D" then "🇩" else if c == "E" then "🇪" else if c == "F" then "🇫" else if c == "G" then "🇬" else if c == "H" then "🇭" else if c == "I" then "🇮" else if c == "J" then "🇯" else if c == "K" then "🇰" else if c == "L" then "🇱" else if c == "M" then "🇲" else if c == "N" then "🇳" else if c == "O" then "🇴" else if c == "P" then "🇵" else if c == "Q" then "🇶" else if c == "R" then "🇷" else if c == "S" then "🇸" else if c == "T" then "🇹" else if c == "U" then "🇺" else if c == "V" then "🇻" else if c == "W" then "🇼" else if c == "X" then "🇽" else if c == "Y" then "🇾" else "🇿"

@label "Country flag"
@description "Derive a country's flag emoji from its ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code (US → 🇺🇸). Pure projection: the two Regional Indicator Symbol letters for the code, concatenated. The source of truth for a country's flag — replaces the baked `_flag` field on the country reference rows (storage-as-effect Phase 3c, D5 slice 3)."
@tags "geo" "country" "flag" "emoji" "storage-as-effect"
countryFlag : (code: String) -> String
countryFlag code = concat (regionalIndicator (slice code 0 1)) (regionalIndicator (slice code 1 2))
